Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.29,0:00:38.89,Default,,0,0,0,,It's time to
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.67,0:00:41.91,Default,,0,0,0,,JuJuJuJooJuJooJUUUNje
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.07,0:01:06.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Would you like to meet my friends?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.45,0:01:08.29,Default,,0,0,0,,They'd love to meet you.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.39,0:01:14.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, girls, give Herr Joseph\Na warm welcome, won't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.43,0:01:21.09,Default,,0,0,0,,You see, this magic card allows me to\Nsummon every Valkyrie I hold in my hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.33,0:01:22.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Valkyrie?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.25,0:01:25.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, and unfortunately\Nfor you, I have four.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.53,0:01:26.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Four masters at once?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.03,0:01:29.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you plan on repeating everything I say?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.47,0:01:32.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Because that's going to get\Nirritating rather quickly.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.39,0:01:41.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, if I may continue, my Fraulein\NFawcum has some business to take care of.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.61,0:01:44.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's begin with my\Nfavorite Valkyrie, shall we?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.77,0:01:48.81,Default,,0,0,0,,She's known as Valkyrie Zwei and\Nshe has quite the special ability.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.47,0:01:51.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Whenever she's summoned to the field,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.51,0:01:54.86,Default,,0,0,0,,one of my opponent's monsters\Nis automatically destroyed.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.77,0:02:04.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, if you'll turn your attention\Nto Bachelorette number two.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.45,0:02:08.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Her interests include horseback\Nriding and long walks on the beach.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.31,0:02:09.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.22,0:02:11.72,Default,,0,0,0,,And stealing other\Nmonsters' attack points.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.07,0:02:15.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Monsters that have been\Nremoved from play, that is.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.23,0:02:20.25,Default,,0,0,0,,And since your Jinzo had a strength\Nof 2400, so does my Valkyrie.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.55,0:02:23.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, for the fun part.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.09,0:02:26.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Attack his life point with Galloping Gash.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.15,0:02:28.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.47,0:02:30.24,Default,,0,0,0,,One more attack and he's done!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.37,0:02:32.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Right you are.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.87,0:02:35.65,Default,,0,0,0,,So let's finish this off\Nwith my triple threat.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.47,0:02:38.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks for playing.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.01,0:02:41.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, man!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.29,0:02:42.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey lost the door!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.01,0:02:44.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Look on the bright side.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.11,0:02:48.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Kaiba Corp may have some\Nlovely parting gifts for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.81,0:02:51.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't think that's\Ngonna be necessary, pal.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.51,0:02:53.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey's still in the duel! But how?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.01,0:02:56.27,Default,,0,0,0,,No one could survive that onslaught.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.37,0:03:00.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Unless, of course, they happen to have a\Nhandy little magic card in their corner.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.49,0:03:02.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Like Hyper Refresh, for instance.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.91,0:03:08.20,Default,,0,0,0,,It doubled my strength right before\Nyour little pony sisters attacked me.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.25,0:03:13.67,Default,,0,0,0,,So my life points never hit zero.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.79,0:03:18.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Which means I'm still\Nin the game, Zig Freak.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.37,0:03:20.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, but that won't last long.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.77,0:03:24.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I place one card face\Ndown and end my turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.17,0:03:28.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Luckily for you, my Valkyries\Nmust now clear the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.91,0:03:30.81,Default,,0,0,0,,And back in my deck they go.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.67,0:03:35.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, ladies.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.81,0:03:37.34,Default,,0,0,0,,It's been such a pleasure.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.49,0:03:39.05,Default,,0,0,0,,We must do this again soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.13,0:03:41.45,Default,,0,0,0,,You can talk to your cards\Ntill you're blue in the face.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.53,0:03:44.17,Default,,0,0,0,,You're still not going\Nto win this duel, Yuge.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.25,0:03:46.47,Default,,0,0,0,,You're wide open and it's my move.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.27,0:03:50.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Mr. Keibel,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.49,0:03:52.39,Default,,0,0,0,,we've isolated the virus and rebuilt the
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.47,0:03:55.01,Default,,0,0,0,,mainframe hard drive If\Nyou'll do the honors,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.09,0:03:56.86,Default,,0,0,0,,we'll be back in business, sir
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.63,0:03:59.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Initiating backup system
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.71,0:04:04.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.62,0:04:05.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, it's fixed
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.77,0:04:08.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, where was I?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.01,0:04:14.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Finally, the heat's off I'd\Nhate to see the gas bill
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.79,0:04:18.26,Default,,0,0,0,,I should check with Seto and see what's up
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.53,0:04:26.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Congratulations, Herr Kaiba You stopped\Nmy virus and saved the day Or so you think
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.13,0:04:32.49,Default,,0,0,0,,It looks like the computer whiz kid That
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.57,0:04:35.28,Default,,0,0,0,,broke into my father's\Ncompany Is all grown up
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.17,0:04:40.59,Default,,0,0,0,,And he's back to his old tricks again
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.65,0:04:43.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Roland
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.09,0:04:46.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Run another background\Ncheck on Siegfried Lloyd.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.05,0:04:50.40,Default,,0,0,0,,I need to know if he's connected\Nto the Schroeder family.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.65,0:04:52.57,Default,,0,0,0,,You think he planted that virus?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.83,0:04:57.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know what to think, but right\Nnow that freak is my number one suspect.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.57,0:05:00.23,Default,,0,0,0,,He reminds me of a kid that I once met.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.13,0:05:05.35,Default,,0,0,0,,A kid with the most dangerous\Nprogramming skills I've ever seen.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.07,0:05:10.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.31,0:05:11.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Time is money.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.93,0:05:13.22,Default,,0,0,0,,That thought is cheap.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.01,0:05:14.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Look out.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.92,0:05:18.29,Default,,0,0,0,,First, I'll summon my Swordsman\Nof Landstar in attack mode.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.13,0:05:23.81,Default,,0,0,0,,And now, attack his\Nlifepoints directly, buddy.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.65,0:05:27.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you really think\Nit would be that easy?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.61,0:05:30.19,Default,,0,0,0,,I activate Fricka's Mediation.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.55,0:05:37.61,Default,,0,0,0,,All I had to do was remove\Na card from the grave.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.25,0:05:41.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, your Swordsman's\Nattack has been neutralized.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.61,0:05:42.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Big deal.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.83,0:05:45.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll place one card face\Ndown and end my turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.55,0:05:47.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm in shock.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.15,0:05:49.07,Default,,0,0,0,,And why's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.09,0:05:53.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Beating you is more fun than I thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.79,0:05:55.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Just go.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.01,0:05:59.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Fine, I'll begin by\Nactivating this magic card.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.73,0:06:00.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Nibelung's Treasure.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.15,0:06:04.59,Default,,0,0,0,,This affords me the ability\Nto extract another magic
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.67,0:06:08.39,Default,,0,0,0,,card from my deck and place\Nit on your side of the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.93,0:06:11.59,Default,,0,0,0,,So I present Nibelung's Ring.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.99,0:06:14.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Und I also draw five cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.31,0:06:17.25,Default,,0,0,0,,So what's the deal with the ring?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.51,0:06:20.97,Default,,0,0,0,,There's no need to thank\Nme, just consider it a gift.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.53,0:06:24.67,Default,,0,0,0,,But we'll talk more about\Nmy generosity a bit later.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.39,0:06:28.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I must call upon the\Nthree divine sisters.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.95,0:06:44.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Now it's one underdog against three divas\NYou mean four divas Now let the fun begin
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.69,0:06:50.93,Default,,0,0,0,,with the goddess Skull Activate your\Nscepter of revelation Und foresee the future
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.67,0:06:54.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Each turn from now on\NI'm able to seize the
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.55,0:06:56.73,Default,,0,0,0,,top three cards in your deck Und rearrange
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.81,0:07:02.81,Default,,0,0,0,,them any which way I please That's not fair\NJoey's future isn't looking too bright,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.95,0:07:03.78,Default,,0,0,0,,guys
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.85,0:07:08.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Interesting cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.15,0:07:12.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's start by placing\Nthe middle one on the top.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.13,0:07:15.11,Default,,0,0,0,,then the first card,\Nand then the third, eh?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.03,0:07:19.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't see what good that's\Ngonna do, but it's your call.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.25,0:07:22.77,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll understand once I\Ncall upon Goddess Verdanda.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.09,0:07:26.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Her Scepter of Guidance\Ngives me the opportunity to
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.05,0:07:29.53,Default,,0,0,0,,guess what type of card\Nrests on top of your deck.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.61,0:07:31.53,Default,,0,0,0,,If I happen to guess correctly,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.61,0:07:36.07,Default,,0,0,0,,then you're forced to play that\Ncard face down on the field. No way!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.35,0:07:40.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I will go out on a limb here\Nand say, Your top card's a monster!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.93,0:07:43.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Since you're the one that put\Nit there, I'm not too impressed.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.81,0:07:47.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, either way, you have to summon\Nit face down, so let's have it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.81,0:07:48.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Whatever.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.31,0:07:54.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Finally, I call upon\NGoddess Earth. Each turn,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.63,0:07:59.47,Default,,0,0,0,,she gives me the opportunity to guess the\Nidentity of one of your face down cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.61,0:08:02.63,Default,,0,0,0,,If I'm right, it's removed\Nfrom play. Say what?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.85,0:08:04.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me take a wild guess.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.53,0:08:07.03,Default,,0,0,0,,It's Panther Warrior.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.97,0:08:09.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like I'm right.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.21,0:08:13.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Aw, parting is such\Nsweet sorrow, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.17,0:08:18.21,Default,,0,0,0,,First he took out Jinzo and\Nnow it's Panther Warrior?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.29,0:08:20.35,Default,,0,0,0,,But those are Joey's best monsters.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.57,0:08:21.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Not anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.09,0:08:24.53,Default,,0,0,0,,I think I've done enough damage.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.97,0:08:25.95,Default,,0,0,0,,So go.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.41,0:08:29.53,Default,,0,0,0,,And if you could step it up\Na bit, I'm getting bored.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.61,0:08:30.65,Default,,0,0,0,,It's official.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.93,0:08:33.81,Default,,0,0,0,,He is the most annoying\Nopponent I've ever faced.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.11,0:08:35.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, look out! Hold on!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.85,0:08:37.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I almost forgot about my gift!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.51,0:08:39.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Eh? Your what?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.85,0:08:42.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Have you forgotten about\Nthe ring I gave you?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.61,0:08:45.49,Default,,0,0,0,,It allows you to draw\Nan extra card each turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.99,0:08:47.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Any reason why you're helping me?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.03,0:08:51.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, it also prevents the\Nmonster wearing it from attacking.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.23,0:08:54.43,Default,,0,0,0,,How did I guess?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.67,0:08:57.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Anyway, on with the duel!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.65,0:08:58.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, where was I?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.93,0:09:01.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Getting intercepted by me again.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.77,0:09:04.23,Default,,0,0,0,,You've activated the curse! Curse!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.77,0:09:06.85,Default,,0,0,0,,The curse of Nibelung's ring.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.21,0:09:10.15,Default,,0,0,0,,If either of the two cards\Nyou just drew is a monster,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.23,0:09:13.31,Default,,0,0,0,,the ring forces you to send\Nit straight to the graveyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.39,0:09:14.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait, hold on.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.61,0:09:16.13,Default,,0,0,0,,There's no need to check.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.41,0:09:19.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks to my goddesses, I\Nalready know you drew a monster.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.95,0:09:23.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Namely, Knight of Dark\NDragon. You're right!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.15,0:09:24.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.07,0:09:27.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Now off to the grave it goes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.93,0:09:32.03,Default,,0,0,0,,He's eliminating Joey's\Nbest monsters one by one!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.15,0:09:37.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I have a feeling that's been Siegfried's\Nstrategy since the beginning of the duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.93,0:09:40.51,Default,,0,0,0,,He's using his magic ring\Nand his three goddesses
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.59,0:09:43.71,Default,,0,0,0,,to dismantle Joey's\Ndeck one card at a time!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.81,0:09:53.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks to those three goddesses of his,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.19,0:09:56.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Siegfried knows what card\NI'm gonna draw before I do.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.39,0:09:57.67,Default,,0,0,0,,But not for long.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.39,0:10:01.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I activate Dangerous Machine Type 6.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.13,0:10:06.23,Default,,0,0,0,,This should keep things interesting.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.31,0:10:09.97,Default,,0,0,0,,See, I'm gonna give this little gadget\Na spin before each one of my turns.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.05,0:10:12.93,Default,,0,0,0,,And what it does to you depends\Non what numbers come up.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.01,0:10:16.42,Default,,0,0,0,,So you're depending on Lady\NLuck to win this duel for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.77,0:10:19.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I guess you can't depend\Non skill now, can't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.69,0:10:22.63,Default,,0,0,0,,It took more than luck to\Nget me where I am today.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.79,0:10:24.37,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'm about to prove it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.53,0:10:26.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold that thought. My move.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.47,0:10:30.97,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the part where you show me\Nyour top three cards. Excellent.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.27,0:10:35.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Now place the second card on top,\Nthen the first, then the third.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.33,0:10:39.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Now to guess your top card,\NI'll say Goblin Attack Force.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.75,0:10:44.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like Lady Luck's on my side.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.69,0:10:48.51,Default,,0,0,0,,If he doesn't stop Siegfried\Nsoon, he'll run out of monsters.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.93,0:10:52.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I place this face down and end my turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.83,0:10:54.93,Default,,0,0,0,,You think he's so cool?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.01,0:10:55.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Watch this.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.39,0:11:00.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, thanks to my ring, that\Nmonster in your hand is destroyed.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.73,0:11:01.73,Default,,0,0,0,,That may be true.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.97,0:11:06.79,Default,,0,0,0,,But now it's time to give the old one-armed\Nbandit a spin and see where things land.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.87,0:11:10.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, big bucks, no whammies. Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.83,0:11:14.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like I can activate\Nspecial effect number three.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.25,0:11:17.89,Default,,0,0,0,,This lets me draw an extra card,\Nso now I get to pick up two.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.41,0:11:22.83,Default,,0,0,0,,So please give a warm\Nwelcome to my Sasuke samurai.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.47,0:11:29.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Mm-mm-mm, your Samurai Shrimp is useless.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.19,0:11:33.97,Default,,0,0,0,,That scrawny swordsman can't\Npossibly get past this card!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.09,0:11:35.92,Default,,0,0,0,,What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.09,0:11:38.01,Default,,0,0,0,,It's my Logi's Flame Trap.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.13,0:11:39.97,Default,,0,0,0,,But as long as it stays in play,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.05,0:11:43.83,Default,,0,0,0,,monsters with 2,000 points or\Nfewer can't attack me. Oh, well.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.09,0:11:46.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Guess I'll play my face-down card.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.35,0:11:48.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, Graceful Dice!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.55,0:11:59.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I get to multiply my samurai's\Nattack points by the number I roll.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.45,0:12:02.23,Default,,0,0,0,,He needs a five or a six. Come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.89,0:12:05.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.99,0:12:07.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.15,0:12:11.97,Default,,0,0,0,,You are so terrible at this game,\NI actually find it frightening.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.11,0:12:13.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.29,0:12:21.19,Default,,0,0,0,,You beat me fair and\Nsquare, mate. Good on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.91,0:12:25.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I just want to say to\Nmy adorable boyfriend...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.73,0:12:27.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Yugi, I did it!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.63,0:12:29.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Alright, Ziggy.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.95,0:12:32.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Before you start guessing all my cards,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.13,0:12:35.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm going to pick out a mystery\Ncard just to keep you on your toes.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.95,0:12:38.77,Default,,0,0,0,,So I'll just place this\Nlittle number face down.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.85,0:12:39.73,Default,,0,0,0,,And that's all.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.89,0:12:42.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Then it's time for my\Ngoddesses to do their thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.79,0:12:44.27,Default,,0,0,0,,so show me your cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.57,0:12:47.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Place a middle card on top of your deck.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.11,0:12:56.05,Default,,0,0,0,,And yet another one of your\Nmonsters disappears never to return.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.81,0:12:59.91,Default,,0,0,0,,This seems like a good\Ntime to play my magic card.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.23,0:13:01.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Swan Maiden.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.63,0:13:04.89,Default,,0,0,0,,This lets me summon one\NValkyrie from my hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.29,0:13:12.53,Default,,0,0,0,,She's too powerful.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.79,0:13:13.99,Default,,0,0,0,,He'll lose the duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.27,0:13:15.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Attack now!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.99,0:13:19.47,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not over yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.87,0:13:22.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I play my silver dollar trap.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.65,0:13:26.33,Default,,0,0,0,,It can protect any monster with\N1,000 attack points or less.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.47,0:13:29.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I love it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.87,0:13:32.75,Default,,0,0,0,,A rich snob gets stopped\Nby a measly dollar.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.13,0:13:35.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I see you did something\Nright for a change.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.31,0:13:41.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Enjoy it, because I assure you this brief\Nstreak of luck won't last too much longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.71,0:13:45.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, here goes nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.53,0:13:51.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll kick things off by activating\Nmy Dangerous Machine Type 6.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.33,0:13:55.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Now show me some love.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.49,0:13:57.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.71,0:13:59.89,Default,,0,0,0,,That means I draw an extra card, baby.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.97,0:14:02.07,Default,,0,0,0,,And it looks like I'm on a roll.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.29,0:14:03.23,Default,,0,0,0,,No pun intended.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.53,0:14:06.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Because now I get to activate\Nmy Magic Card Roll of Fate.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.85,0:14:12.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, whatever number I roll, that's how\Nmany cards I get to draw from my deck.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.31,0:14:16.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Jackpot!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.01,0:14:19.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Check this out!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.89,0:14:23.99,Default,,0,0,0,,My giant trunade blows every\Nmagic and trap card off the field!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.33,0:14:28.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I play
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.47,0:14:31.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Apple of Enlightenment!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.31,0:14:32.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.63,0:14:35.29,Default,,0,0,0,,That trap card should have\Nbeen blown off the field!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.37,0:14:39.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Apple of Enlightenment automatically\Nactivates when it's taken off the field,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.35,0:14:42.76,Default,,0,0,0,,which allows me to draw I draw\None more card from my deck.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.01,0:14:47.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Plus, when my Logis' Flame leaves the\Nfield, it allows me to activate this card.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.21,0:14:49.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Valkyrie Brunhilde!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.85,0:14:56.41,Default,,0,0,0,,She gains 300 attack points for every\Nwarrior and dragon monster on the field,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.53,0:14:57.81,Default,,0,0,0,,including yours.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.63,0:14:59.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Not for long!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.01,0:15:04.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I sacrificed my Swordsman of\NLandstar to summon maximum six!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.93,0:15:11.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Now whatever number I roll is multiplied\Nby 200 and add it to his attack points.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.47,0:15:17.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like he gets an extra 1,200 points.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.09,0:15:23.67,Default,,0,0,0,,And since I'm feeling lucky, I'll\Nplay my Star Blast Magic card.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.19,0:15:27.77,Default,,0,0,0,,The higher he rolls, the\Nstronger a monster I can play.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.03,0:15:31.09,Default,,0,0,0,,But first, I have to\Nsacrifice my Suzuki Samurai.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.89,0:15:33.69,Default,,0,0,0,,And away we go!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.67,0:15:37.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Nice!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.93,0:15:41.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Since my samurai had two\Nstars and I rolled a five,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.79,0:15:43.97,Default,,0,0,0,,I get to summon a seven-star monster.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.29,0:15:46.83,Default,,0,0,0,,So go, red eyes, red dragon!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.07,0:15:54.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, Maximum Six, take out his\NValkyrie with lightning fist attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.49,0:15:58.39,Default,,0,0,0,,No way!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.65,0:16:00.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Why wasn't she destroyed?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.59,0:16:02.59,Default,,0,0,0,,It's called a special ability.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.01,0:16:08.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Brunhilde avoids destruction by\Ngiving up a thousand defense points.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.91,0:16:09.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Fine!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.82,0:16:10.72,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, red eyes!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.93,0:16:13.59,Default,,0,0,0,,You get rid of us with Inferno Fire Blast!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.53,0:16:23.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I'll activate my Trap again.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.25,0:16:29.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I've embarrassed you enough, so I'll\Nplace this card down and call it quits.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.45,0:16:32.77,Default,,0,0,0,,With only a hundred points\Nleft, this is your last shot!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.55,0:16:36.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Nice comeback, dude! You rock! Good job!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.39,0:16:42.68,Default,,0,0,0,,You should have ended this\Nduel when you had the chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.99,0:16:45.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Now prepare to pay the price.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.65,0:16:49.91,Default,,0,0,0,,This duel's gone on long enough,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.19,0:16:54.71,Default,,0,0,0,,so I activate the magic card\NEnchanted Sword Noothout!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.03,0:16:58.05,Default,,0,0,0,,It raises Brunhild's attack\Npoints by four hundred!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.73,0:17:05.71,Default,,0,0,0,,According to the legend of Nothung, it\Nwas the world's greatest dragon slayer.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.85,0:17:07.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Say what? It's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.75,0:17:12.93,Default,,0,0,0,,With one fell swoop, this sword can\Nremove every single dragon from play.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.53,0:17:15.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Not my red eyes!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.07,0:17:20.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Next I play my final card\Nand the key to my victory.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.51,0:17:23.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Rainbow Bridge of Bifrost.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.65,0:17:29.59,Default,,0,0,0,,So my Valkyrie gains 500 attack points\Nfor every monster I remove from the game.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.79,0:17:30.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I get it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.73,0:17:34.26,Default,,0,0,0,,He's been planning this\Nfrom the beginning.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.41,0:17:37.19,Default,,0,0,0,,That's why Siegfried removed\Nall of Joey's monsters.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.27,0:17:39.15,Default,,0,0,0,,To power up his own.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.37,0:17:45.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Now his Valkyrie is strong enough\Nto wipe out Joey's life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.73,0:17:50.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold your horsey.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.33,0:17:52.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I play compensation mediation.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.23,0:17:56.21,Default,,0,0,0,,So, you're relying on luck again?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.37,0:18:00.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, pal, I think you're scared\Nbecause I never lose at these things.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.43,0:18:02.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Now choose any two cards\Nfrom your graveyard and
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.03,0:18:05.97,Default,,0,0,0,,shuffle them together with\Nmy Mediation Trap card.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.39,0:18:09.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I get to pick one card.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.93,0:18:12.27,Default,,0,0,0,,And if I choose mine, I'm safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.39,0:18:16.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, and should you fail,\Nthen I win the duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.49,0:18:20.19,Default,,0,0,0,,I know you can do this.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.79,0:18:23.11,Default,,0,0,0,,And the card I pick is...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.19,0:18:24.75,Default,,0,0,0,,The middle one
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.31,0:18:31.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.51,0:18:40.37,Default,,0,0,0,,It looks like your luck has run out\NNow, Hilda, my dear End this duel
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.75,0:18:49.95,Default,,0,0,0,,No way!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.93,0:18:52.17,Default,,0,0,0,,This can't be!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.25,0:18:53.29,Default,,0,0,0,,He lost!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.65,0:18:58.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Her Joseph, some things\Nin life just never change.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.17,0:19:03.19,Default,,0,0,0,,A rose is a rose, and a loser is a loser.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.21,0:19:08.01,Default,,0,0,0,,And the winner of this\Nbout is Siegfried Lloyd!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.41,0:19:13.07,Default,,0,0,0,,And with that, the grand championship\Nis down to its final four duelists.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.43,0:19:15.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Big deal.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.71,0:19:18.83,Default,,0,0,0,,So you blew the entire tournament\Non a lousy game of chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.91,0:19:21.44,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess you must have\Njust run out of luck.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.25,0:19:25.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Nah, Joey wins his duels with\Ntalent, not with luck, guys.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.81,0:19:28.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, so Joey didn't lose\Nbecause he has no luck.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.15,0:19:30.09,Default,,0,0,0,,He lost because he has no talent.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.29,0:19:32.21,Default,,0,0,0,,So that's how you cheer me up?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.55,0:19:35.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Then it's time for me to spread\Na little cheer on my own!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.59,0:19:40.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey did a great job.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.65,0:19:44.37,Default,,0,0,0,,And sooner or later, he's going to\Nlearn to control that temper of his.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.45,0:19:45.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Probably later.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.07,0:19:48.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I get no respect at all!
